## SQ-RPS-01 | isolated boot: ladder loads clean, nested mods found
@group B
@commands Boot with `rps only`. `grep -nE "Diet ladder|Raspberry Pie|solapplepie|solcarrot|Mixin apply|Missing or unsupported" logs/latest.log` (RPS-01)
@pass exactly one `Diet ladder: 47 rungs, 4 slots, 11 pool effects` info line; no `Diet ladder (` warning line (V12 included); no `APPLE PIE SETTINGS RASPBERRY PIE CANNOT WORK WITH` block; no missing-dependency, mixin or injection error; `Done (` reached
@fails nested jar metadata or version range in `mods.toml` / `ce.forge-bundle.gradle` (P1); default ladder file (P2); a mixin target that needs a mod the standalone set lacks (P4, P6)
@from plan_rp_standalone.md section 6
bootexpect Diet ladder: 47 rungs, 4 slots, 11 pool effects
bootreject Diet ladder \(
bootreject APPLE PIE SETTINGS RASPBERRY PIE CANNOT WORK WITH
bootreject Missing or unsupported mandatory|InvalidInjectionException|Mixin apply.*solraspberrypie.*failed|MixinApplyError|Encountered an unexpected exception
look the `Diet ladder:` line appears once in the whole log (grep -c); the line reads exactly `Diet ladder: 47 rungs, 4 slots, 11 pool effects`
## CQ-RPS-02 | isolated client: names, Apple Pie book and potato recipe gone, book recipes work
@group client
@commands Client with `rps only`, new survival world. Inventory, `/recipe`-free: open the crafting table and JEI-free recipe book; craft book + bread, book + apple juice or any drink, book + carrot (RPS-02)
@pass the book is named Diet Log, the second book Food Dictionary (not Apple Pie's names); Apple Pie's own book recipe and its potato recipe are absent; book + food gives a Diet Log, book + drink a Liquid Diet Log
@fails Raspberry Pie `assets/solraspberrypie/lang/en_us.json` and `client/LangOverrides.java` (names, P4: the lang file holds `solraspberrypie.override.item.solapplepie.food_book` "Diet Log", `solraspberrypie.override.item.solcarrot.food_book` "Food Dictionary", `solraspberrypie.override.key.solapplepie.open_food_book` "Open Diet Log"; `client.ClientLanguageMixin` copies each `solraspberrypie.override.<key>` onto `<key>` after all lang files merge, so Controls also shows "Open Diet Log"); `RecipeManagerMixin` (recipe removal must run without KubeJS)
@draft client steps: crafting-table slots, names read by the capture driver
## CQ-RPS-03 | isolated client: no diversity table, Apple Pie food values stand, tooltips and books agree
@group client
@commands Client with `rps only`, no diversity file on the classpath. Eat or inspect bread, apple, golden apple, cake; open the Diet Log (RPS-03)
@pass no table loaded (one INFO line `No diversity table (solraspberrypie/diversity/*.json) in any mod; Apple Pie's values apply`, no warning); each food's tooltip diversity value equals Apple Pie's own value for it; the Diet Log shows the same value after eating
@fails `Diversity` loader (P3): no-file case must not override; the tooltip mixin reading a different source than the book
@draft client steps and the reference values (read Apple Pie's own tooltip values from the nested jar)
## SQ-RPS-04 | loose Apple Pie 2.2.0 beside the nested copy: one loads, no crash
@group B
@modset rps loose
@commands Boot with `rps loose` (loose `solapplepie-1.19.2-2.2.0.jar` in `mods/` next to the nested one) (RPS-04)
@pass server reaches `Done (`; no duplicate-mod crash and no `ModFileDuplicate`/`Duplicate` error; the log names one `solapplepie` mod file; one `Diet ladder:` line
@fails Jar-in-Jar version range in `ce.forge-bundle.gradle` (P1); Forge picks the higher or loose version: both are 2.2.0, so the nested jar must be skipped without an error
bootexpect Done \(
bootexpect Diet ladder: 47 rungs, 4 slots, 11 pool effects
bootreject Duplicate|duplicate mod|ModFileDuplicate|DuplicateModsFoundException|Encountered an unexpected exception
look `grep -n "solapplepie" logs/latest.log` shows one loaded mod file for solapplepie
## CQ-RPS-05 | Apple Pie defaults: eat, respec, drop, die; ageing-out and gate
@group client
@commands Client with `rps only` (Apple Pie settings at their defaults: `queueSize` 32, `minFoodsToActivate` 0). Eat a run of different foods past 32 entries, respec at the ladder screen, drop a food, die (RPS-05)
@pass eating adds diversity; `minFoodsToActivate` 0 opens the gate at the first meal; a respec moves the oldest window foods to count 32 and diversity falls by exactly what they gave (6.1); death moves the whole window out (diversity 0, `resetOnDeath` false); with `endDecay` 32 = `queueSize` 32 the moved foods are forgotten at the next meal, so the Diet Log shows no older-foods history (expected, not a FAIL); start log has no boxed `APPLE PIE SETTINGS RASPBERRY PIE CANNOT WORK WITH` warning and exactly two INFO lines from `Raspberry Pie`: `Apple Pie settings: endDecay 32 is not below queueSize 32: foods aged out by respecs and death are forgotten at the next meal ...` and `Apple Pie settings: Apple Pie's own benefit list is not empty; Raspberry Pie keeps it off (its ladder replaces it)`
@fails ageing-out cost and gate in `raspberry_pie.md` 6.1 and the gate code (P5); `logic/ApplePieSettings.java` (P5)
@draft client steps: eat loop with `/give`, respec command, `/kill`
